00:43:23.546 --> 00:43:25.730
is sort of a natural example of

00:43:25.731 --> 00:43:30.610
something from economic theory known as Delegation.

00:43:30.611 --> 00:43:32.740
Delegation is a- which actually

00:43:32.741 --> 00:43:33.590
dates back to one of

00:43:33.591 --> 00:43:34.730
the first articulations of the theory.

00:43:34.731 --> 00:43:36.615
Delegation was actually in the Nobel laureate

00:43:36.616 --> 00:43:37.805
Ben Tolstrooms PhD.

00:43:37.806 --> 00:43:39.405
thesis from the 1970s.

00:43:39.406 --> 00:43:42.160
Delegation is a very constrained form of

00:43:42.161 --> 00:43:44.870
the broader topic of Mechanism Design.

00:43:44.871 --> 00:43:46.510
And Mechanism Designing principle

00:43:46.511 --> 00:43:47.950
makes up a set of rules for

00:43:47.951 --> 00:43:49.400
a game that agents play and they're

00:43:49.401 --> 00:43:51.690
trying to create a certain behavior.

00:43:51.691 --> 00:43:53.590
But Mechanism Design tends to

00:43:53.591 --> 00:43:55.180
involve things like monetary transfers,

00:43:55.181 --> 00:43:57.615
where you reward people differently for what they do.

00:43:57.616 --> 00:43:58.970
Delegation says we have

00:43:58.971 --> 00:44:00.450
a situation where all the principal

00:44:00.451 --> 00:44:03.030
can do is refuse to accept certain solutions.

00:44:03.031 --> 00:44:04.420
They send the agent out to search for

00:44:04.421 --> 00:44:06.770
a solution, but they say,

00:44:06.771 --> 00:44:10.020
"I'll reject solutions with the following predicate,

00:44:10.021 --> 00:44:12.435
and so you have to find something that passes my filter."

00:44:12.436 --> 00:44:14.160
And by constraining the agent's action

00:44:14.161 --> 00:44:15.200
they're actually trying to

00:44:15.201 --> 00:44:18.285
actually create a better solution by recon and price.

00:44:18.286 --> 00:44:19.530
